  <name>DICOM Compressed Round-Trip Test Channel</name>
  <description>Phase 22 / CVE-09 / D-13 hard gate: DICOM Listener source (inbound C-STORE) +
    DICOM Sender destination (dedicated DcmRcv SCP stub), proving compressed transfer syntaxes
    (JPEG2000 Lossless Only 1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.90, JPEG Lossless Process 14 SV1
    1.2.840.10008.1.2.4.70) negotiate and relay end to end through the DIMSE connector after
    the jai_imageio.jar -> jai-imageio-core/jpeg2000 1.4.0 swap. Unlike dicom-roundtrip-test.xml
    (nativeData=true, Implicit VR LE only), this Listener leaves defts/nativeData/bigEndian at
    their all-false default so DICOMReceiver.onStart never calls dcmrcv.setTransferSyntax(...),
    and the inherited org.dcm4che2.tool.dcmrcv.DcmRcv#NON_RETIRED_LE_TS default (which already
    includes JPEGLosslessNonHierarchical14 + JPEG2000LosslessOnly, verified directly against
    DcmRcv.java:139-149/229 this plan) is used for negotiation instead. No PixelData-mutating
    transform (kept deliberately absent — the acceptance gate is transfer-syntax/SOP-class/tag
    PRESERVATION, not mutation); DICOMSerializer's toXML/fromXML round-trip on encapsulated
    pixel data was live-verified byte-identical for both fixtures before this channel was
    written (22-04-SUMMARY.md D-12 spike). Test-only; never deploy to production.</description>
